      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "What is now Lopatcong Township began as Phillipsburg Township on March 7, 1851, carved from parts of Greenwich and Harmony.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lopatcong_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Morris Canal, completed in 1836, ran alongside Lopatcong Creek, linking the area to Jersey City.",
